    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the sole test class `AcceptanceTest` runs green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date, responding with HTTP 400, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/RequireNotFutureRegistrationDate.java` \u2014 a guard step that reads the validated `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` and throws a checked `FutureRegistrationDateException` when `registrationDate` is after `LocalDate.now()`. An omitted date is left alone (it defaults to the server date in `BuildOwner`).\n- `rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateException.java` \u2014 checked exception carrying the supplied and server dates.\n- `rest/escalation/FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing `CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler` style.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` \u2014 maps the exception to its handler.\n\n**Wiring:**\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `notFutureDate` step between `validate` (which publishes the DTO) and `identity`, so an invalid future date is rejected early, before the owner is built or saved.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `registrationDate: 2999-01-01` and expecting 400) passes, and the full suite is green.",
